WEBVTT

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.740
Day four of the Reapers' Game, huh.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.090
Will anything change
if I survive this game?

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.710
I don't know if things will change,

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.050
but I don't want to give up.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.380
On what?

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.260
My dream.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.190
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:08.940
SHIKI

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:12.570
Shibuya's so diverse.
All kinds of people come here.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.240
I hate Shibuya.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.700
Everyone's wrapped up in themselves,
making a racket.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.450
Just like Noise.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.920
Yo! So, this is where you were.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.670
The walls over by Ten-Four are gone today!

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.550
Beat! Rhyme!

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.300
Everywhere else is blocked, though.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:36.390
Anyway, what are you guys doing over here?

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.310
Looks like you're buddy-buddy now.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.720
We are not.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.980
We were people-watching.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.560
Oh. Scanning them freaks me out, y'know?

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.110
All those people all
thinking different things.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.030
Yeah.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:56.280
Everyone's values are
colliding at crazy speeds.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.740
Shibuya's packed with people,
but nobody notices us.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:02.790
Yeah.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.580
It makes me kind of lonely.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.500
That so?

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.460
In the Underground,

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.540
no one notices me.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.960
No one talks to me.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.220
I don't have to talk with anyone.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.220
Y'know, you say some real gloomy stuff.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.310
You OK?

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:24.600
Yeah. Talking with people is pointless.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:30.480
Scanning just tells me what they think.
It's nice and easy.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.780
There's something... lonely about that.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:39.570
I think it's better to talk and
learn to understand each other.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.080
Yeah?

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.580
Yeah.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.870
Your stuffed animal's adorable.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.620
You mean Mr. Mew?

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:48.750
Mr. Mew?

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:51.750
Yeah. I made him.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.000
Wanna touch him?

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.550
Yeah!

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:55.590
Wow!

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.050
Mmm! Soft and fluffy!

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.970
You're amazing, Shiki!

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:01.470
I made this outfit, too.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.600
Huh?

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.510
I'm impressed.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.720
Yeah.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.190
I want to be a fashion designer.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.520
It's great to have a dream.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.280
I don't really know what
it's like to have a dream.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.280
You "don't know"? You just don't have one.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:21.660
Hey, Phones!

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.160
Watch your temper, Beat!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:34.800
Listen, Rhyme, just keep moving and
you'll find a dream before you know it.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.050
So, it don't matter if
you ain't got one now.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.050
I'm gonna be the best
skateboarder in the world!

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:44.890
OK!

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:48.560
Someday, I'll find a dream of my own.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:51.560
Isn't that pendant really rare?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.110
I lined up for it with friends,
but I couldn't get one.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:59.070
It was a birthday present
from my big brother.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.660
Wow. You've got a great brother.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.660
Yup!

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.370
He's super nice.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.290
I'm really proud of him.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.540
I hear there's an event at Ten-Four!

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.880
What?

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:13.960
Hey, hear that?

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:15.090
Let's go!

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:17.420
Hey, what's got everybody so worked up?

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.840
They're heading toward Ten-Four.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.140
We haven't gotten a mission.
Wanna check it out?

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:27.640
If it ain't a mission, I ain't interested.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.980
Oh, wait up, Beat!

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:33.310
Sorry. See you later.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.730
There they go.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.230
What about you?

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:43.280
I'll go if you want to.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.910
Whoa! What's with this crowd?!

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.910
This is normal for Ten-Four.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:55.380
Oh! They've got new outfits in!

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:58.630
Wow! These are totally cute.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:01.420
Hey, Eri, what do you...?

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.090
Eri?

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.260
Sorry.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.220
I used to come here with friends.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:08.180
What the--?!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.470
Oji!

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.970
Eiji!

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.650
Who's that guy?

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:16.650
That's Eiji Oji.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:20.860
He's really taken off recently thanks
to his don't-give-a-damn attitude.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:27.070
Keep it down.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.240
All he did was drink water.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.250
They say, "The Prince sells."

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:35.960
Everything Eiji Oji compliments
sells out in no time.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.750
He even pushed that pendant
Rhyme had on his blog.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.170
You waited in line for it, right?

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.340
He kind of influenced me.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:50.260
When it comes to fashion,
his comments are spot-on.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.060
Now you mention it,
you said you made your clothes.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.060
They look store-quality.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:07:00.690
I only sewed them. The designs are Eri's.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:04.280
I want to make clothes for a living.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:08.740
I want lots of people to wear our clothes.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.830
And I want them to make people happy.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.950
That so?

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.040
Yup!

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:17.880
Hey, mind if I take
another look at that shop?

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.080
Nope.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:26.880
Is that why you're trying so hard?

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.970
If you survive these seven days,

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:33.720
will your dream come true?

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:40.060
"Free Spain Hill from the Noise"?

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:42.400
Spain Hill

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.280
Enough is enough!

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.910
They keep coming!

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.450
Someone might be attracting Noise.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.620
Neku! Those two!

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.750
Ai, are you mad?

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.710
I told you I'm not.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.840
Liar! You're totally mad!

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:06.420
I'm not lying!

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.760
I'm telling you, I'm not mad!

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.760
So many Noise!

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:10.800
How do you make things get<i> that </i>bad?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.140
Looks like those two
are the cause this time.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:17.980
No matter how many we erase,
new Noise keep coming.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:20.310
I'll figure something out.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:22.310
Neku, take out the Noise around us!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.980
Sure! I'm on it!

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.580
Get down!

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:44.800
Why are they fighting like this?

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:47.170
I can't believe she's hiding it.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.970
I know that Mina was meeting with Makoto.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:56.060
Not good. I'm pretty sure
Ai's got the wrong idea.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:59.480
Trying to surprise her might've backfired.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:02.270
OK, I'm going to use Imprinting.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.400
What's that?!

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:10.570
It means using your Player pin
to speak directly to people's minds.

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.580
Please, talk to each other
and work this out.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:23.710
I know you and Makoto have
been meeting up in private!

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:26.090
You caught on? That figures.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:29.090
Why are you acting so calm when--?

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:30.840
Here you go.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.180
What're these?

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:34.140
Don't change the subject!

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:38.180
I want to go to a 777 concert with you.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:39.020
What?

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:41.100
You wanted to go, right?

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:47.320
You see, Makoto and I were thinking
up a surprise for your birthday.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.150
A surprise?

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.900
Sorry I suspected you!

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:55.450
It wasn't easy getting tickets, you know.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:56.910
I'm really sorry.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.450
Thanks, Mina!

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.540
Neku! There's no more new Noise!

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:03.750
Yeah!

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.880
Those're the only ones left!

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:15.140
Run!

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.200
We did it!

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.830
Yeah.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.620
Let me treat you to something.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.870
And it looks like those two
managed to make up.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.870
For real? I want a parfait, then.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.080
You got it!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.790
What a pain.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.460
No, it's not.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:53.880
Friends can help each other when
they're sad or in trouble, and...

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:55.050
Eri, what're you doing later?

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.680
I haven't decided.

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:58.760
L-Let's go that way, Neku.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:10:59.970
Wha--?

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.680
Hey! Hey, what's gotten into you?

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:05.560
You haven't mentioned that girl lately.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.560
Nothing. Just hurry.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.900
Oh, you mean Shiki.

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:14.110
She looks just like you!

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.450
It's... kind of complicated.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:19.660
If something's on your mind, I'll listen.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:22.580
I-It's because...

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:25.460
...I'm Eri here.

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:33.630
So, day five.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:37.090
Hey, you OK?

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.050
Sorry.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:41.050
I might not be up to much today.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.270
Why not? What's going--?

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:49.020
"Dominate the Scramble
Crossing view at 3:00."

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.310
"Dominate the view"?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:53.230
Three hours from now?

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.860
That's just not enough time!

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:58.780
Come on, Makoto. Make it work.

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:03.290
We're playing the ad here at 3:00.
That's already set in stone.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:08.080
Set things up so everyone's eyes
are locked on it for me, OK?

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:12.710
B-But if we just play the video,
everyone will walk right by it.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.460
Hey, could that be today's mission?

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.010
Hey.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:19.890
Oh, sorry.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:22.300
I was spacing out.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.850
Because of that girl we passed?

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:27.810
Yeah.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.650
That was Eri. I told you about her before.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:36.440
She's cute, and smart,
and everyone likes her.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:39.990
I... wished I could be her.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.290
That makes no sense to me.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:54.670
Didn't you say you wanted to cheer
people up with the clothes you made?

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.460
I...

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.590
Shiki.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:02.220
I think you're fine being you.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.350
Let's clear this mission.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:10.270
Yeah.

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:15.520
But what are we gonna do to clear it?

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.320
We use Eiji Oji.

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:19.610
Everyone listens to that guy.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.950
This water's totally delicious.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:23.990
The Prince knows his stuff!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:26.030
That's that water from yesterday, right?

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:26.030
It's just water, right?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.790
I only got it because you
waited in line for me, Sota.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:30.580
Yup. We might learn something
about Oji if we scan them.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.580
I'm super glad, you know.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:31.830
R-Really?

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.880
Thanks, Sota.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:39.260
Looks like Oji's holding
an event at AMX later.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.140
We're giving out all of these?

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.050
You got it.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:47.350
My boss is pressuring me
to spread 'em around.

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:49.390
That aside...

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:52.560
...these things look like red skulls.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.110
Damn!

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:57.320
Why's there another wall here?!

00:13:57.320 --> 00:13:59.570
We're already short on time!

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:02.490
I wonder what we have to do to open it.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.280
There's no Noise around.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:08.160
Huh? What?

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.660
The requirements have been met.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.460
I'll release this wall.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:17.540
The wall's gone.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.090
Go. Take care of that pin.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.260
Huh?

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:25.180
What was that about?

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:28.890
He told me to
"take care of that pin," right?

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:32.140
My pocket glowed just now.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:35.730
What pins do I have that you don't?

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:39.440
The pin you got from that band Reaper.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.570
Oh, that one!

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:46.530
Still, 777 is a Reaper, right?

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:49.620
I wonder if that means
some Reapers are nice.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.290
Huh?

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:54.670
Why've you got two Player pins, Neku?

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:57.630
Player Pins are supposed
to be one per person.

00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:02.550
How should I know? I don't even
know why I'm playing this game.

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:04.720
Oh, umm...

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:07.090
Having two might come in handy!

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:12.310
Like, the spare pin in your pocket
might stop a bullet, or something.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.350
Sounds like you've bounced back.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:17.860
Huh? What?

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:21.320
Hey, Neku, what do you mean?

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:34.200
Thank you for today!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.910
Last night,

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:40.210
I was lost in thought,
drinking this delicious water,

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.670
when it hit me.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.800
Red Skull pins!

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:48.840
What would happen if you all put these on?

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.220
We made it.

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:55.270
Yes! It'd be the birth of a new trend!

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:59.100
Come on, everybody!
Let's start a trend together!

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.100
OK.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.730
I'll use Imprinting.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:06.450
At 3:00, look at the
giant screen at Q Front.

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:07.700
I know!

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.490
Put on Red Skull pins,

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:15.080
and then go watch the
giant screen at Q Front at 3:00!

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:16.830
It'll be our promise.

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:29.550
At 3:00 today, please watch the
giant screen at Scramble Crossing!

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:30.970
Huh?

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:33.560
The crowd's growing.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.430
Looks like it worked.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.640
I hope so.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.060
Oh! Makoto!

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:39.650
Huh? Ai?

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:41.900
Hi there.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:41.900
Those girls are...

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:45.230
I'm <i>so </i>sorry. She found out
about the surprise, and...

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.780
That's great.

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:48.740
Two birds with one stone again.

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.200
You might be right.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.530
It's 3:00.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:10.220
What's going on?!

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:11.720
Look at that!

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:20.770
What's that thing?

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:22.230
Is that a Noise?

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:24.980
Hey, no one warned me about that thing!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.280
Wasn't that enough to clear the mission?!

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:46.590
It's hopeless.

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:47.960
We're done for.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:08.190
What...

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.740
...just happened?

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.990
Looks like we cleared the mission.

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:17.580
So... we're safe for now?

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:20.040
It seemed different from usual.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.120
Yeah.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:24.460
A lot of other Players got erased too.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:27.170
One wrong move, and we'd have joined them.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:32.420
You've been saving my neck all day, Neku.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.340
I need to shape up.

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.930
I think... you're doing fine.

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:43.560
With that part-timer,

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:46.270
and those schoolgirls yesterday,

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:49.900
we won because you didn't abandon people.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:52.360
Plus...

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:56.370
...you didn't give up on me,
even after what I did.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:19:00.700
Lots of people have been saved
'cause of things you did.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:03.870
So, you're pretty...

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:05.170
...amazing.

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.420
Thanks, Neku.

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:12.800
You've changed a lot in a short time.

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:14.590
Have I?

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.970
I just...

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:20.260
...never want to screw up like that again.

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:23.680
Don't worry.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.270
You're fine, Neku.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:31.530
You seem down today, Eri. You OK?

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:32.530
Yeah.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:35.400
Sorry. I know we're here to have fun.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.780
If something's wrong, I'll listen.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.070
OK.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.330
You see,

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:43.870
I'm thinking of giving up
designing completely.

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:42.620
Hey!

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:44.710
What?!

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:47.080
Why?! You're so good at it!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.170
Eri, why?

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:52.210
If you're curious, just scan her.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:55.720
I could never do something like that.

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:59.010
I loved the outfit you
showed me the other day.

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:59.800
I couldn't peep at my friend's thoughts.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:02.100
I want to see more of your designs.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:02.100
She'll never know about it.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:03.600
Thanks.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:03.600
It's easy.

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:05.140
You're wrong.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:09.810
The thought of finding out
what Eri really thought of me...

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.110
...scares me.

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:16.610
Didn't you say you were going
to be a fashion designer?

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:19.070
I can't do it without Shiki.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:22.950
Shiki's incredible.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:26.250
She turns the smallest ideas
into complete clothes.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:30.580
She's skillful, sensitive,
and a hard worker.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:33.840
I think she had more talent than me.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:36.630
But I couldn't find
the right way to tell her.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:39.050
I really hurt her.

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:44.140
You see, Shiki was worrying that she
wasn't good at designing clothes.

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:48.850
So, I tried to downplay it.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:52.270
I said, "You're not meant
to be a designer."

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:54.940
"You're a great seamstress, anyway."

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.320
I wanted to apologize right away.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:02.160
I was going to say sorry
first thing the next morning.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:04.950
But now...

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:08.160
...I can never see her again.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:18.170
The clothes I design only become real
when Shiki makes them for me.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.380
So...

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:23.100
...I can't do it without Shiki.

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:27.640
That's how she thought of me.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:29.520
It was our dream

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:34.940
to make lots of people happy with
the clothes we made together,

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.690
but now...

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:41.410
It's still... our dream.

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:46.580
Neku, I'm sure now.

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:49.910
I want to come back to life
and make clothes with Eri.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.790
Excuse me? "Come back to life"?

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.170
Oh yeah.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:56.630
You don't remember that either.

00:21:56.630 --> 00:21:58.670
This is the Reapers' Game.

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:02.430
My entry fee was my appearance.

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:05.930
I don't really look like I do now.

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:09.270
This is how Eri looks.

00:22:09.270 --> 00:22:10.890
What do you mean?

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:16.320
The Reapers' Game is an inspection to
screen Players who want resurrection.

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:18.860
I died in an accident.

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:21.150
Then I'm...

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:23.740
Am I...

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:26.330
...dead?!

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:01.960
ERASED

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.670
Next time: "Erased."
